				<guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/hcusa/</guid>
				<description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;2026, HD video, feature-length&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;div&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;iframe&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;src=&#34;https://player.vimeo.com/video/516513488?dnt=0&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; allow=&#34;fullscreen&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Driven by aspirations of international athletic prestige, a young law student in Detroit bootstraps the formation of a handball team, championing it as “the greatest sport you’ve never heard of.” Realizing that unwavering devotion alone isn’t enough, he is forced to reckon with the choice to pursue athletic accolades or cultivate a community-first organization in a country driven by sports stardom.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
